repository-code: "https://github.com/pantaleonfassbender-coder/Lepanto-and-the-war-for-Cyprus"
url: "https://lepanto-and-the-war-for-cyprus.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the war for Cyprus and the Holy League,
  1570-1573, built from public-domain sources carried in full or in whole
  sections, with the original beside the English: the capitulations of the
  Holy League (Rome, May 1571) in the Spanish copy printed by Dumont,
  transcribed from the page images, with a working translation; Nestore
  Martinengo's report of the siege of Famagusta in William Malim's English
  of 1572, with Malim's dedication, his description of Cyprus and his Latin
  prayer; the captive's tale of Don Quixote I.39 and the prologue to Part II
  in Spanish and English; and Chesterton's Lepanto as reception. With a
  timeline linked into the texts and plates from Stirling-Maxwell's Don John
  of Austria (1883). The Ottoman side has as yet no public-domain English
  source and speaks here only through Venetian, Spanish and English writers,
  a gap the apparatus names.
